%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: TheAncanofrontation
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733785
    - rid: 268099706744733786
    - rid: 268099706744733787
    - rid: 268099706744733788
    - rid: 268099706744733789
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you think Natsuki actually fought a bear?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733790
    - rid: 268099706744733791
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: I don't know; from what {mc} said about the Companions that doesn't seem
      <i>too</i> out of the ordinary.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733792
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 294377bcfa9c68d468fbdb53f597dc39, type: 2}
    dialog: Surely they must've sent help along with her if she really is supposed
      to take down a bear, though.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733793
    - rid: 268099706744733794
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733796
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Huh. You're probably right, Yuri!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733797
    - rid: 268099706744733798
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: It'd be <i>really</i> irresponsible if they sent out a single person
      take down an entire bear-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733799
    - rid: 268099706744733800
    - rid: 268099706744733805
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae40d73afae3081449025561e07b41e5, type: 2}
    dialog: You two! Stop right there!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733801
    - rid: 268099706744733802
    - rid: 268099706744733806
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Is there something wrong, mister?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733803
    - rid: 268099706744733804
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae40d73afae3081449025561e07b41e5, type: 2}
    dialog: Aye, some strange magical-something-or-others have been coming down from
      the college.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733808
    - rid: 268099706744733809
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae40d73afae3081449025561e07b41e5, type: 2}
    dialog: Those stupid mages have been saying it's the fault of some filthy Thalmor-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae40d73afae3081449025561e07b41e5, type: 2}
    dialog: (As if <i>that's</i> what Skyrim needs, mages and elves in the same room...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733810
    - rid: 268099706744733811
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae40d73afae3081449025561e07b41e5, type: 2}
    dialog: But anyway, regardless of whose fault it is, it's dangerous.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733812
    - rid: 268099706744733813
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: Not to worry mister, we're here to help!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733814
    - rid: 268099706744733815
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bd43d09d02697ee489059e7390a0597d, type: 2}
    dialog: We've got just the staff that should help with whatever it is Ancano's
      doing!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733816
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: ae40d73afae3081449025561e07b41e5, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, whatever you do, try not to send the rest of this town down into
      the Sea of Ghosts...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 268099706744733817
    - rid: 268099706744733818
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
